cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Cross-Vendor Disagreement Atlas (CVDA): A 40-Session Production Field Study of Multi-LLM Personality Inference"
abstract: >-
  Lucid is a consumer multi-LLM platform deploying four frontier models
  (Claude haiku-4-5, GPT-4o-mini, Gemini 2.5-flash, Llama 3.3-70b) on the
  same 74-item identity spectrum. Across 40 sessions with all 4 vendors
  completed, only 31.7% of users receive the same MBTI-style type code
  from all 4 LLMs; 68.3% see at least one vendor disagreement. Population
  (N=3,395 sessions, 1,311 analyzed) is 66% AI-skeptical (score_ait ≤ 3
  on 1-7, mean 2.599).
authors:
